[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Dark Mode Implementation (Media and Selector Strategies) in Tailwind CSS"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Dark mode has become an essential feature for modern web applications, reducing eye strain in low-light environments and improving OLED battery life. Tailwind CSS provides robust, out-of-the-box support for dark mode using two primary strategies: the 'media' strategy (OS-level preference) and the 'selector' strategy (manual user toggle)."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites and Configuration"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Before implementing dark mode, ensure you have Tailwind CSS installed in your project. Dark mode behavior is controlled via the 'darkMode' property in your 'tailwind.config.js' file."},{"order":5,"type":"subheading","text":"Strategy 1: The Media Strategy (Default)"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"The media strategy uses CSS media queries ('prefers-color-scheme') under the hood. Tailwind will automatically apply dark styles when the operating system's dark mode is active. This is the default behavior in Tailwind CSS v3."},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"module.exports = {
  darkMode: 'media',
  content: ["./src/**/*.{html,js,ts,jsx,tsx}"],
  theme: {
    extend: {},
  },
  plugins: [],
}"},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Strategy 2: The Selector Strategy (Manual Toggle)"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"If you want to give users a manual toggle to switch between light and dark modes, you must use the 'selector' strategy. This approach relies on a parent class (usually 'dark') being present on the HTML or body element."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"module.exports = {
  darkMode: 'selector',
  content: ["./src/**/*.{html,js,ts,jsx,tsx}"],
  theme: {
    extend: {},
  },
  plugins: [],
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Applying Dark Mode Classes in HTML"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"To apply styles specifically for dark mode, prefix your utility classes with 'dark:'. For example, 'bg-white dark:bg-slate-900' will set a white background in light mode and a dark slate background in dark mode."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"<div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 text-slate-900 dark:text-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-lg">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Card Title</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">This content adapts automatically to the selected theme strategy.</p>
</div>"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Implementing a JavaScript Toggle for the Selector Strategy"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"When using the selector strategy, you need a mechanism to add or remove the 'dark' class from the root HTML element. Below is a standard Vanilla JavaScript implementation."},{"order":16,"type":"code","text":"const themeToggleBtn = document.getElementById('theme-toggle');

// Check local storage or system preference on load
if (localStorage.theme === 'dark' || (!('theme' in localStorage) && window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches)) {
  document.documentElement.classList.add('dark');
} else {
  document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark');
}

themeToggleBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {
  // Toggle the dark class on the html element
  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('dark');

  // Save preference in localStorage
  if (document.documentElement.classList.contains('dark')) {
    localStorage.setItem('theme', 'dark');
  } else {
    localStorage.setItem('theme', 'light');
  }
});"},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices for Dark Mode"},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Avoid pure black (#000000) for backgrounds; instead, use dark shades of gray or slate (like #0f172a) to reduce high contrast eye fatigue."},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Ensure sufficient color contrast ratios between text and background elements to meet WCAG accessibility standards."},{"order":20,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Test your application thoroughly across both system preferences and manual toggles to prevent FOUC (Flash of Unstyled Content)."}]
